1
00:00:07,045 --> 00:00:11,116
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:12,484
Okay.

3
00:00:12,484 --> 00:00:13,418
No power.

4
00:00:13,418 --> 00:00:14,419
Fine!

5
00:00:14,419 --> 00:00:16,221
The cavemen didn't have power.

6
00:00:16,221 --> 00:00:18,957
And they had to deal with
soldiers with machine guns.

7
00:00:18,957 --> 00:00:21,793
And giant aliens with
flamethrowers for hands.

8
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:23,996
If they can do it, so can I.

9
00:00:23,996 --> 00:00:24,863
Yeah, whatever.

10
00:00:25,597 --> 00:00:27,599
But, why did I waste all this
time doing--

11
00:00:27,599 --> 00:00:28,700
YOU!

12
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,068
You told me to go down there!

13
00:00:30,068 --> 00:00:33,038
That, if I turned on the power,
everything would be wonderful!

14
00:00:33,038 --> 00:00:34,239
You're a liar!

15
00:00:34,239 --> 00:00:36,642
I can see why somebody shot you!

16
00:00:36,642 --> 00:00:38,543
I'm taking your gun from you.

17
00:00:38,543 --> 00:00:42,414
I can use this as a drop weapon
if I accidentally shoot a civilian later.

18
00:00:42,414 --> 00:00:44,816
All right, so where do I want to go?

19
00:00:44,816 --> 00:00:50,355
I want to go up, because I've exhausted
every single possible dead end below.

20
00:00:50,355 --> 00:00:52,157
Eh, this jump isn't too bad.

21
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:54,493
And, hey, if I miss,
it won't kill me.

22
00:00:56,628 --> 00:00:59,998
Yeah, I mean, it would hurt, but the
only way a fall like that could kill me

23
00:00:59,998 --> 00:01:03,835
would be if I landed headfirst so that
my body weight snapped my neck.

24
00:01:03,835 --> 00:01:05,170
And that could never happen.

25
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:06,071
I'm a cat!

26
00:01:06,571 --> 00:01:07,305
Meow.

27
00:01:08,373 --> 00:01:09,007
Meow.

28
00:01:10,275 --> 00:01:11,009
Meow.

29
00:01:12,678 --> 00:01:14,046
Mrrrrooooooooowwwww....

30
00:01:16,281 --> 00:01:17,249
HISS!

31
00:01:17,549 --> 00:01:20,118
Okay, I'm just going to slip passed here.

32
00:01:20,118 --> 00:01:23,288
And you're not going to hear me
because you're too bi--OH GOD!

33
00:01:23,288 --> 00:01:24,389
Okay, I'm just going to run now!

34
00:01:24,389 --> 00:01:25,323
Because I'm scared!

35
00:01:25,323 --> 00:01:26,224
You're big!

36
00:01:26,224 --> 00:01:26,658
Running!

37
00:01:26,658 --> 00:01:27,726
[gargantua flames]
Ah-ah-ah-ah!

38
00:01:28,393 --> 00:01:28,994
HOT!

39
00:01:30,128 --> 00:01:32,664
[straining]

40
00:01:32,664 --> 00:01:35,400
I think I underestimated this thing--door.

41
00:01:36,234 --> 00:01:38,970
I can't outrun this, it's got
longer legs than me.

42
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:40,505
Much lo--NO!

43
00:01:40,505 --> 00:01:43,208
God, this happens every time I get cocky.

44
00:01:43,208 --> 00:01:44,509
Somebody like this shows up

45
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:47,779
and I start wishing I hadn't
said a lot of things that I did.

46
00:01:47,779 --> 00:01:49,147
Hey, is that a switch?

47
00:01:49,147 --> 00:01:53,318
Maybe if I press it, it'll beep and
distract this...guy...from me.

48
00:01:53,318 --> 00:01:56,621
Or, I could just walk back and forth in
this cramped hallway for the rest of my life.

49
00:01:56,621 --> 00:01:57,956
That's a viable option.

50
00:01:59,524 --> 00:02:01,059
HEY, GET AWAY FROM THERE!

51
00:02:02,527 --> 00:02:04,029
THAT DOESN'T BELONG TO YOU!

52
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:06,131
Did I even do anything?

53
00:02:06,898 --> 00:02:07,265
Yep!

54
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:09,968
This is like that trick where
the guy runs around on stage

55
00:02:09,968 --> 00:02:11,503
spinning plates on sticks.

56
00:02:11,503 --> 00:02:13,638
[generator powers up]

57
00:02:13,638 --> 00:02:14,740
[generator powers up]
Uhhh...

58
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,540
OW!  Shit.

59
00:02:16,341 --> 00:02:18,510
That did not make a beeping noise.

60
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:20,045
OKAY, THAT'S CLOSE ENOUGH!

61
00:02:20,645 --> 00:02:24,716
Back, back, BACK, BACK, BACK, BACK, BACK,
BACK, BACKBACKBACKBACKBABABAYIYIYIYIYI!

62
00:02:24,716 --> 00:02:25,217
YES!

63
00:02:25,517 --> 00:02:26,918
I MEANT TO DO THAT!

64
00:02:26,918 --> 00:02:27,686
WHOO-HOO!

65
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:31,189
Big reptile thing stomping
around like he owned the place.

66
00:02:31,189 --> 00:02:33,558
Well, that's why the
dinosaurs went extinct:

67
00:02:33,558 --> 00:02:34,459
Me!

68
00:02:34,459 --> 00:02:37,596
The bigger they are,
the cooler they are to kill.

69
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:43,001
Y'know, I'm an expert on electricity
--on the atomic level, anyway--

70
00:02:43,001 --> 00:02:45,737
and this to me looks like the power's on.

71
00:02:45,737 --> 00:02:49,474
A bit more dramatic than what I
was expecting, but still, on.

72
00:02:49,474 --> 00:02:50,909
I'm going back up to that train room

73
00:02:50,909 --> 00:02:53,011
and finding out what
the hell's going on here.

74
00:02:53,011 --> 00:02:55,413
That guard wasn't
telling me the whole story.

75
00:02:55,413 --> 00:02:56,381
What he meant was:

76
00:02:56,381 --> 00:02:58,216
"Hey, yeah, all you have to do is pump out

77
00:02:58,216 --> 00:03:00,485
"all that bilge water in the
generator room,

78
00:03:00,485 --> 00:03:02,220
"turn the power on to the generator,

79
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,688
"shoot everyone in sight,

80
00:03:03,688 --> 00:03:06,224
"then come back on and
turn on the DC generator,

81
00:03:06,224 --> 00:03:08,860
"then go down to the storage
room and roll a spool up here,

82
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:12,597
"then bust out some pliers and electrical
tape so you can lay down some HV cable,

83
00:03:12,597 --> 00:03:15,333
"then, just bust through a wall
and wire up a new circuit,

84
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:17,702
"then do the same thing on the
other end of the complex,

85
00:03:17,702 --> 00:03:20,038
"and, yeah, you'll have that
train running within the month."

86
00:03:20,038 --> 00:03:23,041
Of course, the real tragedy here
is that I didn't bring a camera.

87
00:03:23,041 --> 00:03:24,442
If I had been taking pictures,

88
00:03:24,442 --> 00:03:28,180
I'd be ready when I had to sit through
some family member's slideshow.

89
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,614
I could whip it out and be like,

90
00:03:29,614 --> 00:03:32,350
"Fuck you!  Your pictures
suck! Look at mine!

91
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:35,787
"There's me blowing up some bipedal
alien the size of a dump truck,

92
00:03:35,787 --> 00:03:38,356
"Here's me shooting some troops
because I'm hardcore."

93
00:03:38,356 --> 00:03:41,359
Yeah, I think we're done here.
You brought this on yourself.

94
00:03:42,327 --> 00:03:45,797
Oh!  What's this?
"Power: On"!

95
00:03:45,797 --> 00:03:47,732
It's alive!

96
00:03:47,732 --> 00:03:51,536
I like how we use big Doctor
Frankenstein switches for everything.

97
00:03:51,536 --> 00:03:54,339
That's one thing the engineers
got right around here.

98
00:03:54,339 --> 00:03:58,643
So, now I need to start the
train...which is, not up here.

99
00:03:58,643 --> 00:03:59,811
I'm going to go out the window

100
00:03:59,811 --> 00:04:02,180
because there's no glass and
nobody can yell at me.

101
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,549
That's just one of the perks of
killing everyone.

102
00:04:04,549 --> 00:04:06,218
Speaking of which, if this doesn't start,

103
00:04:06,218 --> 00:04:07,986
I think I'm going to take
it out on that guard.

104
00:04:09,654 --> 00:04:10,922
Ah-ha-ha!

105
00:04:10,922 --> 00:04:12,557
All aboard!

106
00:04:12,557 --> 00:04:15,026
Just kidding, I'm not going to
give rides to anyone.

107
00:04:15,026 --> 00:04:16,761
Wait, wait.

108
00:04:16,761 --> 00:04:18,296
I did it wrong.

109
00:04:18,296 --> 00:04:21,399
That switch controls the track,
not the power.

110
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,467
Let me climb back...

111
00:04:23,268 --> 00:04:24,035
Come on!

112
00:04:27,005 --> 00:04:28,773
Stupid sloped edges!

113
00:04:30,008 --> 00:04:31,443
Fine!  I'll walk.

114
00:04:33,211 --> 00:04:34,679
Eh, screw it, I'll run.

115
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:38,783
The thing about running is that I'm
not really building up any muscle mass,

116
00:04:38,783 --> 00:04:40,418
so it's not like--WAH!

117
00:04:40,418 --> 00:04:43,154
Okay, yeah, the benefits and
drawbacks of running

118
00:04:43,154 --> 00:04:47,392
don't compare to tripping and doing a
faceplant on a white hot burning gas pipe.

119
00:04:47,392 --> 00:04:50,462
That's just about the worst possible
thing I could do, actually.

120
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:53,665
But, yeah, I'm in awesome shape.

121
00:04:53,665 --> 00:04:56,401
And I've been running in circles
today for miles already.

122
00:04:56,401 --> 00:04:57,535
There's just no point.

123
00:04:57,535 --> 00:05:00,438
I'm sure I worked off
those Doritos hours ago.

124
00:05:00,438 --> 00:05:02,507
Hey, you know what?
I don't want to hear it.

125
00:05:02,507 --> 00:05:06,278
Okay, now I'm going to pull this switch
and make my dreams come true.

126
00:05:06,278 --> 00:05:11,816
Or, at least my really unambitious dreams
that I need to happen, like, right now.

127
00:05:13,318 --> 00:05:17,255
Okay, another exciting day in
the life of a forklift operator.

128
00:05:17,255 --> 00:05:19,257
Well, technically this isn't a forklift,

129
00:05:19,257 --> 00:05:22,827
but, I imagine operating an electric
tram is a good stepping stone

130
00:05:22,827 --> 00:05:25,497
towards building a solid
forklift operator career.

131
00:05:26,097 --> 00:05:28,166
You have to aim high.

132
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:29,334
Huh, if I took over the world,

133
00:05:29,334 --> 00:05:32,570
I'd want my henchmen running
around all the time throwing switches.

134
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:35,173
So, this is good because now I can--
Okay, careful.

135
00:05:36,007 --> 00:05:38,310
Because now I can say
I did the same thing.

136
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:41,479
Although, that implies I wouldn't make
people do something I haven't done myself,

137
00:05:41,479 --> 00:05:43,481
which is totally not true.

138
00:05:43,481 --> 00:05:46,952
I'd sacrifice people by the cartload
if it meant I could get better parking

139
00:05:46,952 --> 00:05:48,386
or not have to wait in line.

140
00:05:48,386 --> 00:05:50,121
People pass it off like it's a bad thing,

141
00:05:50,121 --> 00:05:52,290
but I think the Mayans knew
what they were doing there.

142
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:54,292
Yeah, I see you staring.

143
00:05:54,292 --> 00:05:56,394
You'll keep your mouth shut if
you know what's good for you.

144
00:05:56,394 --> 00:05:58,296
You look like you've been gut-shot.

145
00:05:58,296 --> 00:06:00,865
So, you're lucky I don't reach
in and take out your small intestine

146
00:06:00,865 --> 00:06:04,336
and tie it off to use as rope so
I don't have to keep running up here.

147
00:06:04,336 --> 00:06:06,304
I'm not going to do that
because it's gross,

148
00:06:06,304 --> 00:06:09,374
plus I think it'd be too slippery
to get a grip, so be grateful.

149
00:06:10,208 --> 00:06:11,543
Okay, are we going to go?

150
00:06:13,378 --> 00:06:14,913
Yeah!

151
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,982
If I can get out of here fast enough,

152
00:06:16,982 --> 00:06:19,384
maybe I'll still have time to
hit the clubs tonight.

153
00:06:19,384 --> 00:06:20,585
I just need to shower.

154
00:06:21,786 --> 00:06:24,255
Whoa, whoa, whoa.  What's this?

155
00:06:26,257 --> 00:06:29,494
You've gotta be fucking kidding me.

156
00:06:31,963 --> 00:06:34,667
Boy, optimists are retards.

